# SMOKE AND FIRE DURING TAKE-OFF, take-off that can still be aborted (format 1). The checklist is reproduced as printed in the DA50 C / RG Emergency Procedures checklist, Edition 4.1 of 2022-10-05 (owner decisions 2026-10-23 and 2026-10-27): the heading, every item, action and sub-heading as printed. The row marks are the letters A to H of the AFM page that was compared. ASSUMPTION for the owner: the booklet may print numbers 1 to 8 instead; the marks are plain data (the `number` fields), so swapping them is one edit per row plus the typed table in tests/checklist-reference.ts. POWER lever Ground Idle (GI) is the lever position p0; ECS shut-off PULL is the state pulled of the ECS shut-off; Brakes apply is the state applied of the toe brakes; FUEL valve OFF (lift and turn) is the state off of the FUEL selector (the lift is not modelled); Door is graded on the door release lever (state open); the printed row "Airplane evacuate immediately" has no panel action and stays a line. All other text is own wording. The fire constants, the outcome threshold and hold time, the onset window and the forbidden items are copied from ENGINE FIRE in flight and are instructor-review values; the roll starts at 40 knots with full power.
format: 1
id: takeoff-fire-abort
title: T/O FIRE ABORT
source:
  document: "DA50 C / RG Emergency Procedures checklist"
  issue: "Edition 4.1, 2022-10-05"
  section: AFM 03-31 IF TAKE-OFF CAN BE ABORTED
  verified: "2026-10-27"
disclaimer: training-aid
scene: takeoff_roll
briefing:
  situation: "You are on the take-off roll at full power, about 40 knots, with flaps in take-off position. Smoke and flames come from the engine compartment. No message is shown on the primary flight display. There is plenty of runway ahead to stop."
initial:
  controls:
    lv.power: p100
    lv.flaps: to
    lv.gear: down
  quantities:
    fire_intensity: 40
    ground_speed_kt: 40
    airspeed_kt: 40
parameters:
  engine_fire: 1
  ground_roll: 1
annunciations[0]:
checklist:
  form: table
  heading: Smoke and Fire During Take-Off
procedure[10]:
  - kind: comment
    style: subheading
    text: If Take-Off Can Still Be Aborted
  - kind: group
    id: grp_power
    ordered: false
    steps[1]:
      - id: power_idle
        severity: critical
        number: A
        text: POWER lever
        action: Ground Idle (GI)
        done:
          check: state
          control: lv.power
          is: p0
  - kind: group
    id: grp_ecs
    ordered: false
    steps[1]:
      - id: ecs_pulled
        severity: critical
        number: B
        text: ECS shut-off
        action: PULL
        done:
          check: state
          control: lv.ecs_shutoff
          is: pulled
  - kind: group
    id: grp_brakes
    ordered: false
    steps[1]:
      - id: brakes_applied
        severity: critical
        number: C
        text: Brakes
        action: apply - bring the airplane to a stop
        done:
          check: state
          control: lv.toe_brakes
          is: applied
  - kind: group
    id: grp_eng_master
    ordered: false
    steps[1]:
      - id: engine_master_off
        severity: critical
        number: D
        text: ENGINE MASTER
        action: "OFF"
        done:
          check: state
          control: sw.engine_master
          is: off
  - kind: group
    id: grp_fuel_valve
    ordered: false
    steps[1]:
      - id: fuel_valve_off
        severity: critical
        number: E
        text: FUEL valve
        action: OFF (lift and turn)
        done:
          check: state
          control: sw.fuel_valve
          is: off
  - kind: group
    id: grp_elect_master
    ordered: false
    steps[1]:
      - id: elect_master_off
        severity: critical
        number: F
        text: ELECT. MASTER
        action: "OFF"
        done:
          check: state
          control: sw.elect_master
          is: off
  - kind: comment
    style: subheading
    text: After Standstill
  - kind: group
    id: grp_door
    ordered: false
    steps[1]:
      - id: door_open
        severity: critical
        number: G
        text: Door
        action: open
        done:
          check: state
          control: lv.door_release
          is: open
  - kind: line
    number: H
    text: Airplane
    action: evacuate immediately
# The emergency fuel pump would feed the fire and fails the run. It is an instructor-review item.
forbidden[1]:
  - id: emerg_fuel_pump_on
    text: Switch on the emergency fuel pump
    fails_run: true
    trigger:
      check: state
      control: sw.emerg_fuel_pump
      is: "on"
# The outcome ends the run as a fail when the fire stays at a high intensity; the intensity and the hold time are instructor-review values.
outcomes[1]:
  - id: fire_spreads
    text: Fire spreads beyond the engine compartment
    hold_s: 20
    when:
      check: quantity
      quantity: fire_intensity
      op: gte
      value: 85
# The fire of the level Realistic begins at a random second inside this short window; the aircraft rolls at 40 knots from the start (the PFD airspeed starts at the same speed). The window is an instructor-review value.
# The fire shows by its flames and smoke over the cowl, since the scenario lists no message; the lint checks that they show within seconds of the onset.
onset:
  window_s[2]: 2,6
  quantities:
    ground_speed_kt: 40
    airspeed_kt: 40
  cues[1]: flames
